    // to a GITHUB_TOKEN), so the same-token retry is deterministic-
    // forever-failed. With an escalation token wired (App installation
    // token with "Workflows: write", or a PAT with the `workflow` scope)
    // the update retries ONCE with GH_TOKEN swapped to it — the same
    // token-in-env pattern as the silent swap, restored in every finally
    // path (AC7). A second workflows-class refusal surfaces a DISTINCT
    // error naming the missing capability so the caller parks on "needs
    // a workflow-write token", never on a maintainer-edit-revoked trail.
