The UT-4 tests pin the exact env-call sequence. My refactor must preserve:
1. plain: `gh` only
2. silent+restore: set SILENT, gh, set RESTORE
3. silent only: set SILENT, gh, set SILENT
4. escalation success: set SILENT, gh(refused), set ESCALATE, gh(ok), set SILENT (inner finally), set RESTORE (outer finally)
5. escalation refused: ..., set SILENT, set RESTORE (both finallies)
6. no escalation token: [REDACTED:Sensitive Value] SILENT, gh, set RESTORE, throw distinct error
7. non-workflows: set SILENT, gh, set RESTORE, original error

My planned split preserves all of these exactly — helper `_ghEscalatedUpdate(update, silentToken, escalationToken)` does: set(ESCALATE); try update; catch → classify → throw distinct or rethrow eEsc; finally set(silentToken). Outer: try silent; catch classify → if no escalate token throw distinct; return escalated; finally set(restoreToken||silentToken).

Exact error message texts must stay byte-identical (tests assert substrings; keep full messages as-is anyway).

Now write the refactored smProvider code. Current function at lines 847-897 (in merged tree). Let me get exact line numbers and check surrounding helper area to place the extracted helpers, following the file's convention (module-level helpers above githubProvider; the gh-1009 comment says helpers live at module level).

